{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f3d40b89b5aa5a850d11ebb39778b351b79e538e0f772bd0f2707431ae5af013","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar lifecycle cascade","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/lifecycle_cascade.py","src/rebar/_commands/claim.py","src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","cascade_parent_first","_CASCADING_EDGES","ConcurrencyMismatch","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_claim_transition_parent_cascade.py"],"problem_keywords":["code duplication","parent-first cascade","lifecycle state machine","ticket workflow"],"propositions":["The parent-first cascade walk logic is duplicated across claim.py and transition.py; a shared implementation in lifecycle_cascade.py extracts the common walk while keeping decision tables separate.","The cascade must preserve three distinct edges: open→in_progress, closed→open, and closed→in_progress; * → closed must not cascade.","A parametrised test over the live _CASCADING_EDGES table is required to detect future edge additions and prevent silent cascading bugs.","The inbound event cascade from Gerrit 2044 keeps its own write primitive and ordering guarantee; it is deliberately not rewired to the shared implementation.","ConcurrencyMismatch on benign parent races and cycle detection are preserved; the cascade=False replay suppression remains functional."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787412353404956001,"uuid":"8959fcff-d974-4f4f-ad84-360a4d11c487"}